    be ``3`` and dimension along other axes will be same as that of input.

    >>> with jnp.printoptions(precision=2, suppress=True):
    ...   jnp.fft.irfftn(x, s=[3], axes=[0])
    Array([[[ 5.,  7.,  9.],
            [ 6.,  8., 10.]],
    <BLANKLINE>
